 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? Start with a base layer that's roughly your skin tone, or lighter, and wear a hat. Green and blue are safe shades. Avoid any yellow or orange, as they make your skin look colder. For darker tones, add small amounts of yellow or orange near the edges, and little green on top. Mix a small batch the night before, or in the morning, so it' fully mixed and at its best. Restore it daily. Stand a little farther away from the light than you normally would, and take the picture quickly. Slow shutter speeds make the nose and chin disappear.",
